e_step, comment_dispatch, review_request, release/cli, pr/digest, state/unpark) as the indirect ones.; rationale: Both verdicts accept the fixture edit and decide as the plan does; the decision follows them. REVIEW.md lines 23-24 and the gate's test_lock check lock test files from the lock commit on; a fixture line in the reproducing-test commit sits outside that range by the rule's own mechanism, like the two new tests added to the same file, and the intent's constraint is at test level (coding-standards rule 4: no assertion skipped, weakened or deleted). On the one fact the verdicts dispute, the grep over plugin/ confirms the advocate: GITHUB_REPOSITORY_OWNER is read only in plugin/state/unpark.py owner_login, but is_owner_actor wraps it and is called from seven modules, so the plan's 'only reader' line is true for direct reads and too narrow for the blast radius; the safer reading corrects the line and requires the before-the-fix log rather than asserting the pass. The alternatives (actor to `o` in six bodies and asserted strings; owner in the fixture project's sdlc.yaml; the variable in conftest.py against its clean-environment rule) each edit more of tests/ and are worse under the same rules. The by-hand route's --repo fallback is no longer reached by the Go tests; tests/test_owner_rounds.py covers that rule, so this is noted, not parked.; cost: n/a
