++## Flagged concerns
++- decided (decision 35): risk item 'auth': the change adds the owner check to the runbook Go's authorization, the one gate before a running-system action runs with the runbook secrets; the close-look banner shows it and the owner's merge accepts it (at the deploy gate, the owner's approving review).
++- The existing Go tests in `tests/test_detect_cli.py` authorize with the actor `the-owner` on the repository `o/r` and no owner named, so with the fix that actor is not the owner and five of them (the runbook runs, the App refusal's re-run, the route that asked for Go, the head-listed automation identity, the malformed head copy) would fail. The reproducing-test commit, before the test-file lock, must also make the fixture's owner explicit (the `rollback_incident` fixture sets `GITHUB_REPOSITORY_OWNER` to `the-owner` through `monkeypatch`, the pattern `tests/conftest.py` prescribes for a runner variable a test needs); the tests' bodies and assertions are untouched and they pass before the fix as they do today. The intent says "no pre-existing test is edited to make the fix pass": the fixture edit changes no test's assertion and weakens nothing (coding-standards rule 4), but it is an edit under `tests/` that the fix needs, so it is declared here rather than made silently.
++- [x] What happens to a label a non-owner applied: decided the label stays on the pull request and the owner applies their own, per coding-standards rule 2 (match the surrounding code: the bot branch of `_human_label_actor` and the un-park labels of `plugin/state/unpark.py` both leave a rejected label where it is).
++
++## Acceptance
++- A new test in `tests/test_detect_cli.py`: with a `go-requested` rollback route, a `sdlc:go` label applied by a collaborator who is not the owner leaves `performed` false, the reason naming the owner's account, no runbook call, no label change, no runbook record and `runbook_authorized_by` null; it fails on commit `80d7de5cebd4` and passes after the fix.
++- A second new test: the same with the pull request head's `sdlc.yaml` naming the collaborator as `owner`, still refused; and with `owner` named on the default branch, that account's label runs the runbook.
++- Every existing test of `go` passes unchanged in body and assertions (`test_go_by_a_person_runs_the_runbook_and_reruns_the_gate`, `test_go_not_by_a_person_performs_nothing`, `test_go_and_park_refuse_without_the_app`, `test_go_runs_only_a_route_that_asked_for_it`, `test_go_reads_the_automation_identity_from_the_default_branch`, `test_go_fails_closed_when_the_default_branch_copy_is_unreadable`, `test_go_refuses_a_rewritten_origin_and_leaves_the_label`, `test_a_malformed_head_sdlc_yaml_does_not_stop_go_or_dismiss`).
++- `python -m compileall -q plugin tests tasks.py .github/scripts` prints nothing; `python -m pytest` all green; `python -m ruff check . && python -m ruff format --check .` zero warnings.
++- The security-baseline check reports nothing on the diff; no credential in the diff.
++- Mock: none, screens follow the UX conventions
