+## Verdict
+Decide the concern as allowed: the fixture line ships in the reproducing-test commit, before `lock-tests`, and is declared in plan.md; no test body or assertion changes.
+
+## Why
+- The rule is REVIEW.md line 23-24: in a fix-type change the diff must not modify test files that existed before the fix; its deterministic backing is `plugin/gate/checks.py check_test_lock` (line 1851-1883), which fails only on a test path changed between the lock commit and HEAD, and the hook `plugin/hooks/test_file_lock.py` (lines 5-13), which denies test edits from the commit that sets `tests_locked: true` on. `plugin/commands/sdlc-build.md` lines 83-88 commit the reproducing test first and lock afterwards. A fixture line in the reproducing commit is outside the locked range by the rule's own mechanism, exactly as the two new tests added to the same pre-existing file are.
+- The intent's constraint ("no pre-existing test is edited to make the fix pass") and spec R7 are at test level: the five tests named keep their bodies and assertions (`tests/test_detect_cli.py` lines 789-871, 1296-1310, 1689-1709, 2040-2067); `rollback_incident` (line 350-356) is a fixture every one of them already uses, so one `monkeypatch.setenv` there is the smallest edit that names the owner. Coding-standards rule 4 is met: nothing is skipped, weakened or deleted, and the existing tests still prove the owner's label runs the runbook, now against an explicit owner.
+- The pattern is the one `tests/conftest.py` lines 14-21 prescribe: every `GITHUB_*` variable is removed and "a test that needs one sets it itself ... through `monkeypatch`"; `monkeypatch` is function-scoped, so nothing leaks and `tests/test_scaffold.py`'s clean-environment assertion holds. The only reader is `plugin/state/unpark.py owner_login` (line 90; grep over `plugin/`), read before `GITHUB_REPOSITORY`, so the park test's `GITHUB_REPOSITORY=o/r` (line 894) and the rewritten-origin reasons are unaffected.
+- The alternatives are worse by the same rules: changing the actor to `o` edits six test bodies and asserted strings (plan Options not taken); naming `owner` in the fixture project's `sdlc.yaml` on `main` alters the cached fixture repository for every test of the module.
+- Compliance: plan.md "Files that change" names the fixture change in `tests/test_detect_cli.py` and Risks explains it (REVIEW.md line 25-26 satisfied); the adversarial verdict (`evidence/adversarial-review-design.json`, attempted items 9, 10 and 15) checked the count of five and the single reader and found them true.
+- Condition for the build run: the fixture line and the two new tests go in the one `fix(0006): reproducing test` commit, and `lock-tests` runs after it; a fixture edit after the lock would be the Important finding of REVIEW.md line 23 and the gate's `test_lock` failure. The spec's Flagged concerns entry can be ticked `[x]` with this decision.
